prompt the autonomous lap -- reds first, then the lane's own crux
rota lap 4153, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes. The happy zone and the thin edge: a focused check presses on the design where an integrated one presses on nothing. Both of this lap's reds are that lesson from opposite sides -- one guard cost 0s and caught a portability fault a 905s pass had to find, and one guard's own focused control is what proved the repair honest before it shipped.
think The cold pass opened at 07:34 and came back guards_red=2. One was standing_equipment reading its own roster's red, so there was one real red: shell_dialect, verdict=over_sed_i_ceiling, gated_sed_i_sites=1 against a ceiling of zero.
think Following the regex to its site named my own file. tools/fixtures/s/seat_prompt_figure_control.sh line 91 wrote sed -i, landed at 01:43 in ffc82f50d, six hours before the pass that found it.
think GNU sed -i takes no argument and BSD sed -i requires a backup suffix, so the two spellings have no overlap -- which is why the tree keeps sed_inplace in shell_portable.sh, writing a temporary and copying back through the original inode so the tracked mode survives. The control had reached past a helper written for exactly this.
think Repair, then the lane's own crux: REDS %544, my row from the lap before, said shared_pen reads a wipe off the line holding the path, so a wipe naming a variable one line below reads as a hold. The honest population was six wipers and the scan printed four.
think The scan now takes two passes per file. The first collects every variable assigned a constant pen, by the one shape all five spellings share -- a name, an equals, an optional quote, the token. The second reads an rm -rf line naming any of those variables as a wipe of that pen, in the three spellings this tree writes.
obs THE PARAGRAPH THAT DECLINED THE REPAIR MEASURED THE NEED WITH THE READING IT WAS DEFENDING. The scan's own header said a variable tracker was "a cost with nothing to buy" and cited a measurement -- zero files carry that shape now -- taken by the line-scoped reading that could not see the shape. A limitation written down honestly still hides its own size, because the sentence naming a blind spot is written from inside it. This is the second time in two laps that this guard's header taught more than its code.
obs THE REPAIR FOUND EXACTLY THE TWO FILES A HAND-COUNT HAD NAMED, AND NOTHING ELSE. %544 crossed every hold file against a plain grep for rm -r by hand and named ios_app_shell_witness and macos_app_bundle_witness. The two-pass reading named those two and no third, which is the corroboration worth having: a widened meter that finds MORE than the hand-count would have been a new false-positive class rather than a repair.
obs THE CEILING ROSE, AND THIS IS THE ONLY RAISE THIS RATCHET HAS TAKEN. wiping_files 4 -> 6 against a ceiling of 4. Holding four would gate on a number this row proves was measured wrong; raising it says the meter started reading what already stood there rather than that the tree got worse. Both files are LOCA-lane surface witnesses needing a booted simulator, so a Linux pier names them for their owner and does not edit them blind. The ceiling falls to 4 the moment they take mktemp pens.
obs A CHEAP GUARD FOUND WHAT MY OWN GREEN WITNESS COULD NOT. seat_prompt_figure was GREEN before the sed -i landed and stayed GREEN after, because portability is a property no single-host run can see. shell_dialect reads every file in the tree and costs 0s; the pass that surfaced it cost 905s. The transferable rule is that the cheap tree-wide gates -- dialect, ASCII, exec bit, shared pen -- are what a lap ADDING a file owes a run before the send, and they are exactly the ones such a lap never thinks of, since it is watching the guard it wrote.
obs AND THE PRICE OF THAT RED WAS PAID BY EIGHT SHIPS RATHER THAN BY ME. A red guard withholds the roster receipt, so --scoped refuses and every ship pays a full cold pass. One misspelled flag in one control is a fleet-wide tax for as long as it stands, which is why a six-hour red is worth its own row.
obs THE RE-VERIFY WAS KILLED MID-GUARD AND LEFT NO VERDICT. The first pass after the rebase stopped at 08:12 inside rye_witness_walker -- no run_verdict line, no evidence page, the runner gone from the process table while three peers' passes ran on. That is REDS %541 from the other side: a kill matched by program name reaches every ship on the pier. The second pass ran to a verdict in 998s, so the cost was one pass rather than a fact I could not learn.
obs THE REBASE COST FOUR REDS AND NONE OF THEM WAS THE WORK. Landing on five upstream commits took construction/ITINERARY.md to 41,382 against its 40,960 bound, which reddened declared_ceiling and equinox_e123 together -- one root wearing two rows -- and left two shelf rows standing twice, since a rebase re-applies a row without lifting the stale one (%381). The card came back under bound by trimming MY block alone, which is the honest place to cut: eight ships share one budget and whoever pushes last pays it. index_shelf_repair sorted the shelf.
obs AND THE NIB IS THE FOURTH RED EVERY TIME, BY DESIGN. remember_git_nib reds until the card names HEAD's parent, which cannot be written before the commit exists. The pass reads it as a fault and the send closes it, so a lap that reads the pass without knowing that spends a turn on a red that is only a clock.
